+/* Records of their own for tasks pthreads did not make (patches/aros-stuff/0009).
+   An SDL thread (SDL2.module starts them with CreateNewProc and NP_Entry), a
+   Workbench helper or any CreateNewProc'd process that calls pthreads (GCC's
+   emutls does, for every __thread and thread_local) gets a ThreadInfo of its
+   own the first time it asks pthread_self(), in a free slot of the same table:
+   its own TLS values, cleanup list and cancel state. It is "foreign": not
+   joinable (detached, so pthread_join and pthread_detach answer EINVAL), not
+   cancellable (no parent, so pthread_cancel answers ESRCH), and pthread_exit
+   never longjmps out of it.
+
+   OS 3 has no call-back when a task ends, so each foreign record is tied to its
+   task by a token: a one-entry MemList put on the task's own tc_MemEntry list,
+   which RemTask frees with the task. The token's block holds TOKEN_MAGIC, the
+   slot and this program's _threads; the record holds the token's address.
+   A record whose task is gone is found by a sweep: under Disable(), every task
+   on SysBase->TaskReady and TaskWait (and ThisTask) has its tc_MemEntry looked
+   through for this program's tokens, and a foreign record whose token is on no
+   live task's list is reaped: its key destructors run (in the sweeping task),
+   then its slot is free. The token also tells a new task that happens to be
+   allocated where an ended one was from that task: pthread_self() only takes a
+   foreign record whose token is on the calling task's own list.
+
+   The sweep runs when a foreign task registers, at pthread_create and at
+   pthread_key_create, and only if foreign records exist. When the table is
+   full (PTHREAD_THREADS_MAX) after a sweep, the task is the main thread, as in
+   0008, for its whole life: it gets a token for slot FALLBACK_SLOT, so later
+   calls answer 0 at once and it never changes TLS block mid-life. At exit,
+   foreign records are dropped without their destructors (as exit() does for
+   the main thread's values) and this program's tokens are taken off the tasks
+   still running. */
+#if defined(__AMIGA__) && !defined(__MORPHOS__) && !defined(__AROS__)
+#define FOREIGN_RECORDS 1
+#define FOREIGN_LIVE 1
+#define FOREIGN_REAPING 2
+#define TOKEN_MAGIC 0x50546846UL	// 'PThF'
+#define TOKEN_PRI (-97)		// the token MemList's ln_Pri, with ln_Type NT_MEMORY
+#define FALLBACK_SLOT 0x7FFFFFFFUL	// a token for a task that is the main thread (table full)
+#define MAX_MEMENTRY_WALK 64	// a task's tc_MemEntry nodes looked at, at most
+static unsigned numForeign;	// foreign records, live or being reaped (thread_sem)
+static void ForeignSweep(void);
+#endif
